// vib-self Option/Result switch families (docs/SPEC.md §4 "C# validity": on a C#-valid program vib-self reports exactly
// Stage-0's VIB ID set).
// - N19: a switch statement over a place whose labels test the union only inside `not`/`or` (`case not NoneType:`,
//   `case Some<T> or NoneType when ...:`) plus `default:` tests the place without moving it, so a later use of a
//   non-Copy scrutinee is not a use of a moved value.
// - N19 also: an exhaustive union switch whose labels match the CLR union's nominal remainder (`case not NoneType:`,
//   `case Some<T> or not Some<T>:`) does not fall out of the switch in source terms (no false "not all code paths").
// - N21: a guarded wrapper-designation arm (`Some<T> s when g`) over a value scrutinee with a non-Copy payload, followed by
//   an arm that tests the scrutinee again, is VIB005 like Stage-0's move out of the shared match temporary (over a linear
//   union, the N20 ban alone); later arms get no use-after-move cascade.
// - N20: in a switch statement or expression over a linear Option<R>/Result<R, E> value (a call or Move(o); places keep
//   the in-place VIB006), a variant arm may not carry a `when` guard, each variant may be tested by at most one arm,
//   and `not`/`or` patterns are banned: exactly {VIB006}, one per offending arm at the first token of its pattern.
//   `var u`, `_ when ...`, `_`/default and one unguarded arm per variant stay accepted and dispose exactly once.
public sealed class Round12SelfLinearUnionSwitchTests
{
    private const string BanMessage = "A switch over a linear union value may test each variant in at most one arm, without a 'when' guard, and may not use 'not' or 'or' patterns; branch inside the arm instead.";

